    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0418" n="1152" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1152"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-26"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 88.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor, in connection with
                    my note of the 18th instant concerning the proposed restrictions upon the
                    traffic in <pb facs="0419" n="1153" xml:id="pg1153"/> arms and ammunition in
                    Samoa, to inclose for your information a copy of a note addressed to the German
                    ambassador on the 25th instant,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d351-f1"/> in relation to
                    the reported endeavors of the municipal council at Apia “by the issuance of
                    supplementary orders to restrict the right of search,” provided for by the
                    ordinance of August 14, 1894.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
